#!RuleTest
#test CT-RUN-1 expect=violation domain=VS
#note CTD-2 merge — the Trial Summary states TWO CDISC CT versions: both join the run, newest first (D1 "merge, never first-wins"). The runner seeds NY only into the newest package and AGEU only into the older one, so BOTH violations fire only if both TS-derived packages were loaded.
#ct-available sdtmct-2025-03-28 sdtmct-2024-09-27
#expect-ct-mismatch "CT taken from the Trial Summary: sdtmct-2025-03-28 (TSVCDREF \"CDISC CT\", TSVCDVER \"2025-03-28\"), sdtmct-2024-09-27 (TSVCDREF \"CDISC\", TSVCDVER \"2024-09-27\")"
#expectViolationCount 2
dataset VS
col VSSTAT type=Char
col VSAGEU type=Char
---
BOGUS | BOGUS
---

dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
col TSVCDREF type=Char
col TSVCDVER type=Char
---
S1 | TCNTRL | PLACEBO | CDISC | 2024-09-27
S1 | AGEU | YEARS | CDISC CT | 2025-03-28
---
